values
  (211, 'Changes to slice 3.3 after an independent review, before it merged. A wait is recorded only in a turn answering the waiter or the person waited on, never for someone else, and ended, in its thread or the web app, only by the waiter, the person waited on or whoever recorded it; its end and its note in the thread are one transaction. A thread may record at most 20 waits a day besides the ten open, so one person cannot be mentioned without end. Every way Jira can fail (no answer, an error, a body that is not JSON, time running out while it is read) is "Jira did not answer", and `link_task` waits for Jira at most 1.5 seconds, since it runs while the thread''s sync lease is held, then links the key as given. An issue Jira returns from another project (a moved key) is not shown. Jira''s reserved search characters become spaces. The task source is built with storage, so the tasks pages never fall back to the built-in tracker when the agent is not configured. An assignee must be someone the record knows. Left for later: showing a thread''s task on the agents page', 'The review found that anyone in a thread could end anyone''s wait there, that the model chose whose wait it recorded (as 209 found for decisions), that a page from Jira that was not JSON left `link_task` unanswered and retried under the lease, and that the tasks pages could show a second home for tasks. Each now has a test', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-26T00:00:00Z', 'import', '211')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
